      "narrative": "The question hangs in the dim lamplight of the Copper Finch. Mara Venn's fingers pause on the rim of her cup, her sharp eyes studying you with the patience of someone who's been asked this before.\n\nShe sets the cup down. \"The Ash Gate,\" she says, \"has been closed for thirteen years. Since the night the ferryman died.\" Her voice is flat, professional \u2014 a woman reciting facts she's recited before. \"They say Old Bram was the last one to cross through. Came back changed. Dead within the week.\"\n\nShe waits, clearly expecting you to ask the obvious follow-up."
    },
