      "narrative": "Mara Venn's eyebrows lift slightly \u2014 a flicker of respect crossing her face. She tilts her head toward the far corner of the tavern where a man sits hunched over a stack of ledgers, ink-stained cuffs peeking from beneath his coat sleeves.\n\n\"That would be Toran Vex,\" she says, her voice dropping. \"Lockwright of the Kestrel Guild. He maintained the Ash Gate's mechanisms for years. Knows that lock better than anyone alive.\"\n\nToran's head snaps up at the sound of his name. His eyes dart between you and Mara, nervous as a spooked horse.\n\nMara continues, quieter now: \"He's the one who found the lock filed. Woke the whole guild hall screaming about it, or so the story goes. But he's never told anyone what he actually *saw* that night.\" She meets your gaze. \"Maybe you'll have better luck prying it out of him.\"\n\nToran Vex is already shuffling his papers, pretending not to have heard."
    },
