      "narrative": "Mara Venn's fingers drum once against the table. She holds your gaze, then reaches into her coat and produces a folded scrap of paper \u2014 cheap stock, the kind used for market notices.\n\nShe slides it across the scarred wood. On it, a single name is written in cramped, hurried script:\n\n*Sable Quill.*\n\n\"She's a courier,\" Mara says, tucking the paper away. \"Travel-stained cloak, always moving. No fixed address. She'd take coin from anyone who wanted through, lead them to the gate at dusk, and collect her fee on the other side. Old Bram's death didn't slow her down \u2014 if anything, business picked up.\"\n\nMara's jaw tightens. \"She was the last person seen near the gate before the lock was filed. Toran found the damage the morning after she made a crossing.\" She leans back. \"Sable Quill knows what happened to that lock. Question is whether you can find her before someone else does.\"\n\nToran Vex shifts in his seat, his quill scratching nervously against the ledger."
    },
