      "narrative": "The Copper Finch's door swings shut behind you, cutting off the warmth and lamplight. Morning air hits \u2014 damp and heavy, carrying the smell of wet stone and distant woodsmoke. The street is narrow, cobblestones slick with last night's rain.\n\nA short walk takes you beyond the last huddled buildings. The ground rises, and the sky opens grey and flat overhead. There, standing alone against the pale morning, is the Ash Gate.\n\nIt's a cracked black arch, maybe twelve feet tall, set into a low stone wall that curves away into mist on both sides. No hinges. No door. Just the arch, dark as a wound, the stone around it stained with old soot. The ground before it is churned mud \u2014 boot prints layered over boot prints, some fresh, some days old.\n\nA figure stands beside the arch. A courier in a travel-stained cloak, hood drawn up against the damp, one hand resting on the stone as if feeling for a pulse. They haven't noticed you yet."
    },
