      "narrative": "The name leaves your lips and hangs in the damp air \u2014 *Old Bram* \u2014 swallowed by the grey silence.\n\nThe courier by the arch turns sharply, hood shifting, a hand dropping to something at their belt.\n\nBut from the gate itself: nothing. No echo. No whisper. The arch stands mute, a black mouth that swallows sound whole. The mist curls through its opening without resistance, as if the gate leads nowhere at all.\n\nThen \u2014 a scrape of leather on stone. The courier speaks, voice rough and low:\n\n\"You're wasting breath. Bram's been crow-food for thirteen years.\"\n\nThe figure takes a step back from the arch, boots squelching in the mud. \"Who sent you here?\""
