      "narrative": "You drop to a crouch, scanning the churned mud beneath the arch. The morning light is flat, but it catches what the casual eye would miss.\n\nFaint scuff marks scar the stone at the base of the arch \u2014 not the random scrape of boots, but something dragged across the lip. And beside it, a small indentation in the dirt. Rectangular. Clean-edged. The kind of impression a heavy chest or crate leaves when set down and left to settle.\n\nThe courier's cloak draws your eye as they shift weight \u2014 the mud spattered across its hem is a deep rust-brown, nothing like the pale grey slurry underfoot here. That soil came from somewhere else. Somewhere far.\n\nThe courier watches you rise, hood still shadowing their face.\n\n\"Find what you were looking for?\" The voice is flat, unimpressed. \"Or are you just admiring the view?\""
