      "narrative": "The Copper Finch's interior wraps around you again \u2014 copper lamps, scarred tables, the low murmur of early drinkers nursing their breakfast ales. Your old table sits empty, tucked near the back wall where the light from the shuttered windows barely reaches.\n\nYou settle onto the bench. The wood is worn smooth by years of elbows and tankards.\n\nMara Venn is still at the bar, her charcoal coat draped over the stool beside her. She's speaking in low tones with a man you don't recognize \u2014 grey-haired, stooped, his hands wrapped around a steaming cup. He nods once, pushes back from the counter, and shuffles out through a side door.\n\nMara's eyes track you across the room. She picks up her cup and walks over, sliding into the seat across from you without asking.\n\n\"Back already.\" She sets the cup down. \"Either you found nothing, or you found something you don't know what to do with.\" A pause. \"Which is it?\""
